      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "To study potential regional variation in asthma diagnostics, we retrospectively analyzed the management of 800 acutely wheezing preschool-age children in two university clinics in Finland. Multivariate modelling indicated that the place of treatment was a strong independent predictor of asthma diagnosis during acute symptoms. Similar regional preferences in diagnostic activity may exist in other countries."},
